viogpudo: a vertical blank of its own, from a high-resolution timer.

viogpudo leaves every mode's refresh rate "not specified", which a
display-only driver must do when it gives no vertical blank; dxgkrnl then
simulates one, Windows reports 1 Hz, and DWM composes on the 15.6 ms
system tick (64 Hz).  On a 60 Hz host screen that is a frame dropped four
times a second: the Windows 11 desktop's choppiness (2ksbox track M24).

With this patch the driver implements DxgkDdiControlInterrupt and
DxgkDdiGetScanLine (a display-only driver must give both or neither),
reports each mode at VSyncHz with a 1/20 blank, and while dxgkrnl has the
interrupt enabled raises DXGK_INTERRUPT_DISPLAYONLY_VSYNC from an
EX_TIMER_HIGH_RESOLUTION timer, through DxgkCbSynchronizeExecution.
GetScanLine places the scan line by the time since the last tick.

VSyncHz (REG_DWORD) under HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\VioGpuDod
\Parameters, read at DriverEntry: 60 when absent, 0 for upstream's
behaviour exactly, at most 240.  Target modes also get their active size
(upstream copies the total size into it before the total is filled in).

diff --git a/viogpu/viogpudo/driver.cpp b/viogpu/viogpudo/driver.cpp
index 33f18c78..1f2c9404 100644
--- a/viogpu/viogpudo/driver.cpp
+++ b/viogpu/viogpudo/driver.cpp
@@ -46,6 +46,35 @@ int bBreakAlways;
 
 tDebugPrintFunc VirtioDebugPrintProc;
 
+// The vertical blank's rate (2ksbox): VSyncHz under the service's
+// Parameters key, 60 if absent, 0 for upstream's behaviour (no vertical
+// blank of ours; dxgkrnl simulates one and the modes carry no rate).
+ULONG g_VSyncHz = VIOGPU_VSYNC_DEFAULT_HZ;
+
+static VOID ReadVSyncHz(_In_ UNICODE_STRING *pRegistryPath)
+{
+    WCHAR Path[256];
+    if (pRegistryPath->Length >= sizeof(Path))
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+    RtlCopyMemory(Path, pRegistryPath->Buffer, pRegistryPath->Length);
+    Path[pRegistryPath->Length / sizeof(WCHAR)] = L'\0';
+
+    ULONG Hz = g_VSyncHz;
+    RTL_QUERY_REGISTRY_TABLE Table[3] = {};
+    Table[0].Flags = RTL_QUERY_REGISTRY_SUBKEY;
+    Table[0].Name = (PWSTR)L"Parameters";
+    Table[1].Flags = RTL_QUERY_REGISTRY_DIRECT | RTL_QUERY_REGISTRY_TYPECHECK;
+    Table[1].Name = (PWSTR)L"VSyncHz";
+    Table[1].EntryContext = &Hz;
+    Table[1].DefaultType = (REG_DWORD << RTL_QUERY_REGISTRY_TYPECHECK_SHIFT) | REG_NONE;
+    if (NT_SUCCESS(RtlQueryRegistryValues(RTL_REGISTRY_ABSOLUTE, Path, Table, NULL, NULL)))
+    {
+        g_VSyncHz = min(Hz, VIOGPU_VSYNC_MAX_HZ);
+    }
+}
